# Environment Variables
- ALWAYS import env from '@/env' for all environment variable access
- NEVER use process.env.X directly anywhere in the codebase
- NEVER add ! non-null assertions on env vars — t3-env guarantees they exist
- NEVER add ?? '' fallbacks on env vars — use z.string().optional() in env.ts instead
- When adding a new env var: add to env.ts server/client block AND runtimeEnv AND .env.local.example
- Server vars are NEVER prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_
- Client vars MUST be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_
- Exception: process.env.NEXT_RUNTIME in instrumentation.ts is a Next.js internal, not app config

# Database
- ALWAYS use Supabase client from lib/supabase/server.ts or lib/supabase/client.ts
- NEVER use or suggest Prisma
- ALWAYS use getTable() from lib/supabase/schema for table names
- Use server client in server components, actions, and API routes
- Use browser client in client components only

# General
- All secrets are server-only — never import server env vars in client components
